From a8aaafc335f67f6f2db9afaff63c05b682a5beba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:03:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 40/47] Switch: BeginFrame breakdown in perf.log, prefetch
 uploads only with time to spare, skip invisible smoke

- perf.log slow lines split BeginFrame into GPU wait / cache save / buffers /
  sprite requests+uploads and show the slowest texture upload; uploads over
  10 ms get a note. Summaries count frames over 18 ms and over 35 ms.
  (HW test of 8cba57262: two 95-115 ms BeginFrame stalls with 4 uploads and
  only 5-37 ms of GPU wait; this pins them down.)
- Level/class prefetch uploads run only after a frame that made vsync and
  with half the budget; sprites on screen keep the full budget.
- nx_effect_minalpha 0.04 on the Switch: effects below 4% opacity (Brutal
  Doom's fading smoke) are not drawn; each still cost its whole screen area.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
